        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "hmm, keeping just one definition of \"decoded codepoint\" would have been nice, but in general +1 for bias towards \"byte oriented\" thinking as that is how lpeg works internally.\r\n\r\nAlthough, as a more general improvement, since we now \"own\" lpeg it is tempting to teach its engine directly about our chosen concept of a single base character (either _one_ valid UTF-8 decoded codepoint _or one_ invalid byte) in a way that respects \"first byte\" optimizations, but there will be some maintenance burden for that, but just thinking out loud for now...\r\n\r\nLet's not mix in UTF-16 concepts into the picture at all if we can avoid it (for some extremely rare NTFS OS edge case or whatever), just keeping bytes and UTF-8 codepoints in the head is enough cognitive load:P",
